     1,
     "Thanks a lot for your answer. I still I the problem and I really can&#39;t see what to do to solve it.<div><br></div><div>I tried to simplify my data to explain my problem better.</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;white-space:nowrap\"># data</span><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><div># COULEUR VALUES ARE HEXA CODE FOR = yellow, green, red, brown<br></div><div>COULEUR&lt;-c(&quot;#FFFF90&quot;, &quot;#00FF00&quot;, &quot;#FF0000&quot;, &quot;#604800&quot;)<br></div><div>CULTURE&lt;-c(&quot;BLE TENDRE&quot;, &quot;MAIS GRAIN&quot;, &quot;VERGERS&quot;, &quot;SEMENCES&quot;)</div><div>TAUX&lt;-c(0.3, 0.1, 0.4, 0.2)</div><div>df&lt;-data.frame(CULTURE,TAUX,COULEUR)<br></div><div><br></div><div># ggplot code<br></div><div>ggplot(df, aes(x = CULTURE, y = TAUX, fill=COULEUR)) +<br></div><div>  geom_bar(width = 0.9) +  </div><div>  scale_fill_manual(name=&quot;LEGENDE&quot;,values = df$COULEUR, labels=df$CULTURE) </div><div>  </div><div><br></div></span></font></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-zt-aA9OBXbE/T_CknzEI3oI/AAAAAAAAAAo/unv3hJDwB6Y/s1600/image+1.jpeg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-zt-aA9OBXbE/T_CknzEI3oI/AAAAAAAAAAo/unv3hJDwB6Y/s1600/image%2B1.jpeg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375385506000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Fzg9u-80oHt2wYUD_Rncx\"><img src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-zt-aA9OBXbE/T_CknzEI3oI/AAAAAAAAAAo/unv3hJDwB6Y/s320/image+1.jpeg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"282\"></a></p><div>With this code :</div><div>- label doesn&#39;t fit with the data (for exemple BLE TENDRE is red in the data and blue in the label)</div><div>- colours are not conform with their hexacode.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot for your help !</div><div><br></div><div>Anthony</div><div><br></div>"
