  {
   "id": "Uf0yU_aNCXEJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2012-07-01T22:31:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: data and manual colours doesn't fit - how to solve it ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi:\r<br>\r<br>Look at\r<br>\r<br>&gt; str(df)\r<br>&#39;data.frame&#39;:   4 obs. of  3 variables:\r<br> $ CULTURE: Factor w/ 4 levels &quot;BLE TENDRE&quot;,&quot;MAIS GRAIN&quot;,..: 1 2 4 3\r<br> $ TAUX   : num  0.3 0.1 0.4 0.2\r<br> $ COULEUR: Factor w/ 4 levels &quot;#00FF00&quot;,&quot;#604800&quot;,..: 4 1 3 2\r<br>\r<br>Notice that both CULTURE and COULEUR are factors, and observe that\r<br>their default levels are lexicographically ordered. You need to order\r<br>the levels of one of the two factors to be compatible with the\r<br>ordering of the other; one way is to match them using the values =\r<br>argument of scale_fill_manual(), but another way is to reorder the\r<br>levels of one or both of the factors in the data frame prior to\r<br>invoking ggplot().\r<br>\r<br>HTH,\r<br>Dennis\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sun, Jul 1, 2012 at 1:36 PM, Anthony &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">anthon...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Thanks a lot Justine. It works.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; The problem is that this method for scale fill manual is really... manual\r<br>&gt;&gt; ;-)\r<br>&gt;&gt; It seems that my problem comes from the fact that ggplot sort my data\r<br>&gt;&gt; frame from A to Z whereas scale_fill_manual take the data in the same order\r<br>&gt;&gt; as written in the data frame.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Is their an option which could forbid ggplot to sort the data ?\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Regards,\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Anthony\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing\r<br>&gt; list.\r<br>&gt; Please provide a reproducible example:\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375385508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0g_XXsBWEUKf94qhsr9Pyg\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375385508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xry3jjaB86KYyER9Kd2_b\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>"
