  {
   "id": "xMEu_HGb2OcJ",
   "from": "Charlotte Wickham",
   "author": "70ab9fabb9f066d8",
   "date": "2012-07-03T21:33:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: data and manual colours doesn't fit - how to solve it ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Perhaps scale_identity is really what you want (especially if you\r<br>really have more than 4 colour-culture pairs):\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>ggplot(df, aes(x = CULTURE, y = TAUX, fill=COULEUR)) +\r<br>    geom_bar(width = 0.9) +\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "    scale_fill_identity(name=&quot;LEGENDE&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>No legend, but it is redundant in this example anyway.\r<br>\r<br>Charlotte\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
